internal/clock/clock.go:85:24 replace 0 with -1 # equivalent: spendable := math.Max(0, R-M) at clock.go:85 becomes Max(-1, R-M), differing only when D := R-M < 0, where clean gives 0 and mutant gives -1. spendable is read only at clock.go:87 (feedforward = spendable/movesLeft + inc*share, and the bound scaling it) and at clock.go:92 as the argument of math.Max(spendable, SearchMinMoveTimeMs), the upper clamp of clamp(feedforward+corr, SearchMinMoveTimeMs, ...). Since both candidate values 0 and -1 are <= SearchMinMoveMs = config.SearchMinMoveTimeMs (10, and config's own test internal/config/config_test.go:258 asserts floor >= 1), the clamp bounds collapse to lo == hi == SearchMinMoveTimeMs for every input where the mutant differs, so clamp(anything, X, X) = X makes the returned budget identical; the pre-clamp sum may differ but is unobservable. The pid state is unaffected because err at clock.go:89 uses remainingMs and target only, never spendable, so all later Budget() calls match too, and Commit (clock.go:74-82) never reads law(). Verified empirically: a dense sweep (806 remaining values crossing the D=0 and D=1 boundaries in 0.5ms steps plus larger values, moves 0..45, 24 pid states covering primed/unprimed, prevErr in {-600,0,37,60880}, integ at both clamp edges and 0, all 3 time controls) compared clean vs mutated law outputs and post-step controller states: 0 diffs in ~5.4M pairs. Full ./internal/clock suite green with the mutant hand-applied.
